we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-7I & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}-7\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-7I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{10},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-3)I & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-3)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Dividing ${v}_{2}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{10},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the orthogonal matrix $P$ in the usual way, and this gives us the following:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404619 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172026 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4754d4e6-b2d0-5efb-ac92-c004c70004df" :knowledge-point/title "Orthogonally Diagonalizing a 2x2 Symmetric Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c224e271-277d-5f1a-9cc2-c5f3c1736629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $P=\\begin{bm